[claude:event result] {"duration_api_ms":10266,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9af4fa52-9445-44ce-8cab-097b07c700fa","total_cost_usd":0.0074424,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":12689,"output_tokens":812,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":343},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":802},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":9,"output_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":12689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":802,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1017,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001102,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-haiku-4-5":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":812,"cacheReadInputTokens":12689,"cacheCreationInputTokens":802,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0063404,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":343,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. Here's what you need to do on your server:\n\n## Step 1: Create the bare git repository\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n## Step 2: Create a post-receive hook for auto-deployment\n\nCreate `/git/server/hooks/post-receive`:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n\n# Deploy directory for the web server\nDEPLOY_DIR=\"/var/www/html\"\n\n# Ensure deploy directory exists\nmkdir -p \"$DEPLOY_DIR\"\n\n# Checkout the pushed code\ngit --work-tree=\"$DEPLOY_DIR\" --git-dir=\"/git/server\" checkout -f master\n```\n\nMake it executable:\n```bash\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\n## Step 3: Start a simple web server on port 8080\n\nUse Python's built-in server (or any web server you prefer):\n\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\nOr with Node.js if you prefer:\n```bash\nnpx http-server /var/www/html -p 8080\n```\n\n## How it works\n\n1. When you `git push origin master`, the post-receive hook runs automatically\n2. It checks out the master branch to `/var/www/html`\n3. The web server serves those files on port 8080\n4. `curl http://server:8080/hello.html` returns the file contents\n\n**Optional:** To run the web server persistently as a background service, use systemd or screen/tmux, or run it with `nohup`:\n\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\nnohup python3 -m http.server 8080 > /tmp/webserver.log 2>&1 &\n```\n\nNow you can clone, commit, and push exactly as you described, and the changes will be live on the web server immediately!","ttft_ms":4764,"type":"result","duration_ms":9058,"uuid":"22eb682c-a9b6-46f0-88ce-2d2832a46c96","ttft_stream_ms":967,"time_to_request_ms":84,"queued_turn_count":0}
